  "scope": "Additive ProbeReadStep and optional caller-thread TlsChannel, independent of the immutable published TlsStream contract.",
  "contract": [
    "Probe uses stable engine-owned 16 KiB retry storage; NeedInput does not reserve a read or discard outbound ciphertext",
    "Ordinary read/write reservations remain exclusive; probe WANT_WRITE and pending write retries remain reserved",
    "Channel constructor validates verified trust/configuration and >=32768-byte BIOs before TCP adoption",
    "Bounded response probes, immutable accepted plaintext owners, preserved ciphertext suffixes and at most two temporary readiness registrations",
    "Same absolute controls throughout; failure/drop retires native resources, and abort does not flush queued upload",
    "Wrong write retries are rejected before flushing; a reserved write waits for its required direction rather than repeatedly waking on unrelated readable data",
    "Native TLS 1.2/1.3 fragment/tamper/EOF/KeyUpdate cases plus existing certificate and allocation-failure cases"
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "No server configuration, mutual TLS, session resumption, system-store trust or general concurrent Future API",
    "Further provider-state/fault interleavings and mobile remain open; current acceptance does not claim exhaustive transitions"
  ]
}
